From 01822e6b2d98e12eae0f5bd0ca37bd4354630dcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:18:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] FP0104: report writes through a local that is another
 name for a parameter's object

The receiver walk now goes through a local of a type that may be a reference and that is never written
again in the member: a local with an initializer, a foreach variable (an element of the collection) or a
top-level pattern variable of is/case/switch arm (the tested value), when that stands for an access path
(parameter, alias, field/property/indexer/element read, casts, as, !, ?.). Method calls, ranges, new,
with, collection expressions, choices and boxed struct copies end the path. Reported at the target as
written (`same.Total`, `line.Quantity`).

Shared helper: new ancplua-fprog/Shared/LocalAliases.cs, a per-operation-block alias table built once,
lazily and thread-safely. FP0104 now registers its operation actions from an operation-block start action
to own one table per block.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011nXBkinjHz24B8aadiHZjn
